# Roc for Rocci authors

**Prerequisites:** [Prerequisites](/docs/start/prerequisites/). You do not need to be a Roc expert.
**You will learn:** the Roc you will read in `.rocci` files outside template bodies.
**Time:** about fifteen minutes.
**Next:** [Install](/docs/start/install/) if needed, then [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).

This page is not a Roc language manual. Full coverage lives at
[roc-lang.org](https://www.roc-lang.org/). Here is the subset later Rocci
examples actually use.

## Modules and imports

A `.rocci` file is a Roc module. You may write a `module` header, `import`
lines, types, and helpers. Everything outside a recognized `@` declaration is
copied into generated Roc unchanged.

```roc
module CounterPage exposing [hello]

import pf.Html
```

Rocci component names are PascalCase in source (`Hello`). Generated Roc values
are camelCase (`hello`). `exposing` lists and handler bodies use the lowered
name.

## Records, tags, and functions

Props are Roc records: `{ name: "Ada", count: 3 }`. Closed sets use tags:
`[Ready, Working, Failed]` or `[Ok value, Err err]`. Functions are
`name = |args| body`. Pipelines (`value |> f`) appear in helpers.

```roc
Status : [Ready, Working, Failed]

status_label = |status|
    match status {
        Ready => "Ready"
        Working => "Working"
        Failed => "Failed"
    }
```

Prefer `match` when the input is a tag union. Use `if` for a true/false
condition.

## Effects and `?`

Functions that perform I/O end in `!`. `?` unwraps a `Result` and forwards
`Err`. `@component` bodies are pure: no `!`, no logging, no SQLite. Put
effects in `@init` and handlers.

The selected platform for generated standalone apps is the webserver platform
Rocci stages for you (`pf.Html`, `pf.Sqlite`, `pf.Stderr`, and friends). You
do not pick a platform to preview a component.

## What stays Rocci

Markup, `@if` / `@for` / `@match` that produce HTML, `@css`, `@fixture`, and
`@view` / `@patch` / `@command` / `@live` are Rocci syntax. Do not put tags
inside a Roc `{ expr }` interpolation. Convert numbers at the interpolation
site: `{count.to_str()}`.

Continue with [web foundations](/docs/start/web-foundations/) if HTML-over-the-wire
is new, otherwise [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/start/five-minutes/).
